"pro-sumti" should be written with a hyphen, as the "pro" is not a Lojban 
prefix but a Latin one. "prosumti" is a valid lujvo, but it means "an 
argument (of a function or predicate) which opposes something". I think I've 
heard "sumyma'o" or "sumbasti" as a fully Lojban term. "pro-verb" (which is 
much like pro-bridi) is also hyphenated, as a proverb is something entirely 
different.

